  "details": "After updating to VRChat 2025.1.3, we noticed that when an AudioZone has its gain set to 0, lipsync no longer works for the user — even when the microphone is active.\n\nThis did not happen in previous versions.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\n1. Create a world with a VRC_AudioZone.\n\n2. Set the gain value to 0.\n\n3. Enter the zone and speak — lipsync does not activate.\n\nExpected behavior:\n\nLipsync should continue to function as long as the microphone is active, even if gain is 0.\n\nThis affects our VR music live shows where we use AudioZones on stage with gain set to 0.  \n\nSince voice is streamed separately using systems like TopazChat, we want only the lipsync to work without audio playback.  \n\nThis change breaks that setup, which makes it very inconvenient for our production.",
